<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,921,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 22,921,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, meal exports in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 09/18/96    09/11/96     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 22,921,000  24,274,000   24,273,000</p>
<p> Capacity-X	33,990,000  33,990,000   33,842,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	34,637,015  34,637,015	    N/A</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  34,444	66,202	    N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may agree due to rounding by NOPA.  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   09/18/96    09/11/96    Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   3,804,000   4,247,000    4,411,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    3,902,000   4,373,000    4,221,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  3,877,000   3,760,000    4,533,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,470,000   2,152,000    1,598,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,105,000   3,338,000    2,861,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,983,000   4,833,000    4,720,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,780,000   1,572,000    1,929,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	22,921,000  24,274,000   24,273,000</p>
